Z||000032||87ECO5||04-04-2001||03:34 PM||||<B>NDFieroTN</B> - I hear Sunday is the best day to be there (most vendors don't want to pack up the remaining stuff so they offer GREAT deals).  The group I'm going down with will be there all of Saturday and part of Sunday.  In fact, three or four of us will be there Friday afternoon as well.  I've heard it'll be slow at the factory so I'm hoping to hit some of the sites (Space Museum, bars, maybe the Jack Daniel's distillery, more bars, ...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   ).<P><B>tellron</B> - did you get a discount or something?  Six of us are staying at the same hotel and we're being charged $65 + tax per room.<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 04-05-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000033||fiero56||04-04-2001||08:33 PM||||Its April Already?!?! Where have I been? I was thinking it was still months away. I'm never going to finish my 2.8 before the trip. I guess I'll just take my rod-knocking, low oil pressure, no HP, 170K+ mile 2.8 on the 900+mile trip again. Maybe this time we can kill it off! Believe me, I've been trying this past week. The weird thing is: I pushed that engine harder consistantly this past week than I ever have before. 5000rpm shifts, dumping the clutch to see if the Getrag will break or if the clutch will slip, or if the tires will finally break loose, lots of spirited driving, etc. And I STILL got over 30mpg ALL CITY driving(250 miles on 8.2 gallons)! Who needs a Duke when both of my 2.8s can pull numbers that high. ||||reg||1
Z||000034||Songman||04-05-2001||12:43 AM||||Anybody else that is looking for one of these Grooms engines... Keith (Ironhed) is the guy that I have linked on our TN Fieros website. Got an 800 number there so give him a call. He knows his stuff! His little black 88 GT is sporting a Grooms engine.. and we'll be down in Alabama in April wearing our TN Fiero badges! I've almost got the TN Fiero logo window cling logos ready too! <P>That's sort of a different subject, but if you want something cool, trot on down to OfficeMax or any of the other places and buy invent-it! brand clear decals... They are removable, inkjet printable, clear, and great to make logos for your club! About $14 for 10 8.5x11 sheets.. get about 10-12 logos per sheet!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
